                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any tall forward or defensive position (traditionally, full-back, centre half-back, centre half-forward, or full-forward)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "da2a193c-968a-4b22-a16e-bf0142a585eb",
                                                "sense_id": "ea7ae20d-0f51-314b-872a-fb138c3ff6c9",
                                                "text": "Of this year's crop of key position players, the premier tall is Sam Darcy, who stands at 204cm and looms as a future star. Darcy, a father-son for the Western Bulldogs and the son of club great Luke is 7cm taller than his father. Given Luke's great career as a ruckman, it may seem surprising on paper that his son is so much taller than his father, yet is a key position player rather than a ruckman."
